    <informations>Shelly Plus i4DC — schematic symbol.
Terminals, left to right as printed: SW4 SW3 SW2 SW1 ⊥ ⊥ +.

Official sources:
https://kb.shelly.cloud/knowledge-base/shelly-plus-i4dc
https://kb.shelly.cloud/__attachments/a_61979b3326192f0ece3713ae1e3ccd9b32749e1d93c86cf2e9f8a2c0f766c61d/Plus-i4DC.jpg?cb=ac98f2cceb2634df1962c279d3f84652
https://kb.shelly.cloud/__attachments/a_45ae8d994e7eeb5fd52717b4ae31eeb8c490be4e5edcded8f8d8ef742735558d/Plus-addon-interface.png?cb=b6f7e5e1b58d2ac8e3a97827cc15dc11
https://kb.shelly.cloud/__attachments/a_2f4719ba9caa9ef2b5078e01f1edc90f78610fc645ddded9a8bdb47deab7221a/Shelly%20Plus%20i4DC%20multilingual%20printed%20user%20and%20safety%20guide.pdf?cb=b77cbf69456680a416ef8e2b4df79d33

Notes:
- Two physically separate negative supply screws share the grouped ⊥ marking; positive is rightmost.

Nominal dimensions and an illustrative outline: corner radii, screw pitch and recesses are drawn to be recognisable, not to manufacturing CAD.</informations>
